  <header class="privacy-policy__cover">
    <h1>South Africa Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="privacy-policy__eyebrow">Chancen Companion Mobile App</p>
    <dl class="privacy-policy__metadata">
      <dt>Entity:</dt><dd>Chancen South Africa (Pty) Ltd</dd>
      <dt>Effective Date:</dt><dd>19.05.2026</dd>
      <dt>Review Cycle:</dt><dd>Annual (or earlier if required)</dd>
      <dt>Next Review Due:</dt><dd>19.05.2027</dd>
    </dl>
  </header>

  <div class="privacy-policy__body">
    <div class="privacy-policy__document-meta">
      <h2 style="margin-top: 0">South Africa Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> 01.06.2026</p>
      <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> 19.05.2026</p>
    </div>

  <p>This Privacy Policy explains how personal information relating to users located in South Africa is collected, used, disclosed, stored, and protected when you use the Chancen Companion mobile application (the “App”).</p>
  <p>This Policy is issued in compliance with the Protection of Personal Information Act, 2013 (“POPIA”), applicable regulations, and guidance issued by the South African Information Regulator.</p>
  <p>This document supplements the Chancen Companion Master Privacy Policy. In the event of any conflict, this South Africa Privacy Policy Supplement shall prevail for users located in South Africa.</p>

  <section id="about-the-app">
    <h2>1. About the Chancen Companion App</h2>
    <p>“Chancen Companion” refers to the mobile application operated by Chancen that allows users to access program information, including Income Share Agreement (ISA) participation details, communications, career resources, and financial literacy tools.</p>
    <p>The App supports students and graduates participating in Chancen education financing programs and related initiatives.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="responsible-party">
    <h2>2. Responsible Party</h2>
    <p>For users located in South Africa, the responsible party for purposes of POPIA is:</p>
    <address>
      <strong>Khanilor NPC t/a Chancen South Africa</strong><br>
      Registration Number: 2020/689306/08<br>
      Registered Address: 676 Gallagher Avenue, Halfway House, Midrand<br>
      Email: <a href="mailto:companion@chancen.international">companion@chancen.international</a>
    </address>
    <p>As the Responsible Party, Chancen South Africa (Pty) Ltd determines the purpose and means of processing personal information relating to users located in South Africa.</p>
    <p>The technical infrastructure supporting the App may be operated by Chancen International Services. Chancen International Services provides the technology platform and infrastructure that operates the App. However, Chancen South Africa (Pty) Ltd remains responsible for ensuring compliance with POPIA for users located in South Africa.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="information-regulator-registration">
    <h2>3. Information Regulator Registration</h2>
    <p>In accordance with POPIA, Chancen South Africa (Pty) Ltd has appointed an Information Officer responsible for overseeing compliance with POPIA and responding to privacy-related requests.</p>
    <p>Information Officer contact details:<br>Email: <a href="mailto:edwin@chancen.international">edwin@chancen.international</a></p>
    <p>The Information Officer is registered with the South African Information Regulator where required by law.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="personal-information-collected">
    <h2>4. Personal Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>We may collect and process the following categories of personal data:</p>
    <h3>Identity Information</h3>
    <ul><li>Full name</li><li>South African ID Number or student identification details</li><li>Date of birth (where required)</li></ul>
    <h3>Contact Information</h3>
    <ul><li>Email address</li><li>Phone Number</li></ul>
    <h3>Account Information</h3>
    <ul><li>Username and login credentials</li><li>Account activity within the App</li></ul>
    <h3>ISA Program Information</h3>
    <ul><li>ISA participation status</li><li>Repayment obligations</li><li>Payment history</li><li>Balance estimates</li></ul>
    <h3>Device and Technical Information</h3>
    <ul><li>Device type</li><li>Operating system</li><li>IP Address</li><li>App usage data</li><li>Log information</li></ul>
    <h3>Communications Data</h3>
    <p>When you contact support, provide feedback, or interact with the App’s AI chatbot, we may collect the information you share in those communications. This includes messages, questions, and responses exchanged with the chatbot.</p>
    <p>These interactions help us:</p>
    <ul><li>Respond to support requests</li><li>Improve the accuracy and usefulness of the chatbot</li><li>Improve our financial literacy tools</li><li>Enhance user experience and App functionality</li></ul>
    <p>Where reasonably possible, we anonymise or de-identify information before using it for analytics, training, or product improvement purposes in order to protect user privacy.</p>
    <p>This may include:</p>
    <ul><li>Messages exchanged with Chancen through the App</li><li>AI chatbot interactions</li><li>Support requests</li><li>User feedback submissions</li></ul>
    <p>Chancen collects only the personal information reasonably necessary to provide the App and support participation in Chancen programs.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="lawful-basis">
    <h2>5. Lawful Basis for Processing</h2>
    <p>We process personal information in accordance with POPIA and only where processing is justified, including on the following grounds:</p>
    <ul><li>Performance of a contract or taking steps linked to a contract</li><li>Compliance with legal or regulatory obligations</li><li>Legitimate interests of Chancen or the user</li><li>Protection of a legitimate interest of the data subject</li><li>Consent, where required by law</li></ul>
    <p>Personal information is processed in a lawful and reasonable manner that does not unreasonably infringe the privacy of users.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="how-we-use-data">
    <h2>6. How We Use Personal Data</h2>
    <p>Your personal data may be used for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul><li>Providing access to the Chancen Companion App</li><li>Displaying ISA participation and repayment information</li><li>Managing user accounts</li><li>Communicating program updates and notifications</li><li>Providing career, employment, and financial literacy resources</li><li>Maintaining platform security and preventing fraud</li><li>Improving App functionality and user experience</li><li>Complying with legal and regulatory obligations</li><li>Monitoring and improving AI chatbot performance</li></ul>
  </section>

  <section id="isa-account-data">
    <h2>7. ISA Account Data</h2>
    <p>The Chancen Companion App allows users to view information relating to their Income Share Agreement (ISA) participation.</p>
    <p>This may include:</p>
    <ul><li>Estimated ISA balance</li><li>Payment history</li><li>Repayment status</li></ul>
    <p>This information is derived from Chancen’s internal systems, including its Data Warehouse, which stores program and repayment information.</p>
    <p>Balance information displayed in the App may not always reflect real-time updates and should be treated as an informational estimate only.</p>
    <p>The official record of ISA obligations is maintained by Chancen South Africa (Pty) Ltd. Users requiring official balance confirmations should contact Chancen directly.</p>
    <h3>AI Chatbot and Automated Processing</h3>
    <p>The Chancen Companion App may include AI-powered tools and chatbot functionality to assist users with financial literacy, support requests, and general informational queries.</p>
    <p>The chatbot may use automated processing to generate responses based on user inputs. However, important ISA-related decisions are not made solely through automated decision-making without appropriate safeguards.</p>
    <p>Users have the right to:</p>
    <ul><li>Request human intervention</li><li>Request clarification regarding automated outputs</li><li>Challenge or correct inaccurate information generated by automated systems</li></ul>
    <p>These rights are provided in accordance with POPIA protections relating to automated decision-making.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="data-sharing">
    <h2>8. Data Sharing and Third-Party Services</h2>
    <p>Personal information may be shared with trusted third parties where necessary to operate the App and deliver Chancen services.</p>
    <p>These may include:</p>
    <ul><li>Cloud infrastructure providers</li><li>Technology service providers supporting the App</li><li>Payment processing partners (where applicable)</li><li>Legal or regulatory authorities where required by law</li><li>Analytics providers</li></ul>
    <p><strong>AI Technology Partners:</strong> We may use trusted technology providers, including AI service providers such as OpenAI, to process chatbot questions and generate responses.</p>
    <p>Where reasonably practicable, we take steps to remove or mask directly identifying information before sharing data with these providers.</p>
    <p>We do not sell users’ personal information to third parties.</p>
    <p>All operators and service providers processing personal information on our behalf are required to implement appropriate confidentiality and security safeguards in accordance with POPIA.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="cross-border-transfers">
    <h2>9. Cross Border Transfers of Personal Information</h2>
    <p>To operate the Chancen Companion App, some personal information may be processed or stored outside South Africa.</p>
    <p>For example, technical infrastructure or support services may be provided by Chancen International Services in the United Kingdom or by international technology providers.</p>
    <p>Where personal information is transferred outside South Africa, Chancen implements appropriate safeguards to ensure continued protection of personal information in accordance with POPIA.</p>
    <p>These safeguards may include:</p>
    <ul><li>Contractual data protection obligations with service providers and access controls</li><li>Secure cloud infrastructure and encryption</li><li>Technical and organizational security measures</li></ul>
    <p>Cross-border transfers are conducted only where permitted under POPIA.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="data-security">
    <h2>10. Data Security</h2>
    <p>Chancen takes appropriate, reasonable technical, and organisational measures to protect personal information against unauthorized access, loss, misuse, disclosure, alteration and destruction.</p>
    <p>Security measures may include:</p>
    <ul><li>Encryption of sensitive data</li><li>Restricted access controls</li><li>Secure infrastructure and monitoring systems</li><li>Internal policies governing data protection</li></ul>
  </section>

  <section id="data-retention">
    <h2>11. Data Retention</h2>
    <p>Personal information is retained only for as long as necessary to:</p>
    <ul><li>Provide App services</li><li>Support ISA program participation</li><li>Comply with legal accounting, or regulatory obligations</li></ul>
    <p>Retention periods may vary depending on the nature of the data and applicable legal requirements.</p>
    <p>Where users delete their App account through the App settings, Chancen will delete or de-identify App-related personal information within a reasonable period unless retention is required by law or necessary for legitimate business purposes.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="your-rights">
    <h2>12. Your Rights Under POPIA</h2>
    <p>Under POPIA, users have the right to:</p>
    <ul><li>Be notified that personal information is being collected</li><li>Access personal information held about them</li><li>Request correction or updating of personal information</li><li>Request deletion or destruction of personal information where applicable</li><li>Object to certain types of processing</li><li>Withdraw consent where processing is based on consent</li><li>Object to direct marketing communications</li><li>Lodge a complaint with the Information Regulator</li><li>Institute civil proceedings in relation to unlawful processing</li><li>Not be subject to certain forms of solely automated decision-making</li></ul>
    <p>Chancen respects these rights and has procedures in place to help users exercise them.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="exercising-your-rights">
    <h2>13. How to Exercise Your Rights</h2>
    <p>To exercise your privacy rights, please contact Chancen South Africa (Pty) Ltd using the contact details provided below.</p>
    <p>Requests should include sufficient information for us to verify your identity and locate the relevant personal information.</p>
    <p>We will respond within a reasonable time in accordance with POPIA requirements.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="complaints">
    <h2>14. Complaints</h2>
    <p>If you believe that Chancen has processed your personal information unlawfully or failed to protect your rights, you may submit a complaint to the South African Information Regulator.</p>
    <address>
      <strong>Information Regulator South Africa</strong><br>
      Email: <a href="mailto:complaints.IR@justice.gov.za">complaints.IR@justice.gov.za</a><br>
      Phone: <a href="tel:+27100235200">010 023 5200</a>
    </address>
  </section>

  <section id="policy-changes">
    <h2>15. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>Chancen may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect:</p>
    <ul><li>Changes in legal or regulatory requirements</li><li>Changes in technology</li><li>Updates to App functionality</li><li>Operational changes</li></ul>
    <p>Updated versions will be made available within the App.</p>
    <p>Continued use of the App after updates become effective constitutes acceptance of the revised Privacy Policy.</p>
    <p>Where material changes are made, Chancen may provide additional notice through the App or via email.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="contact-information">
    <h2>16. Contact Information</h2>
    <p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how your personal information is processed, please contact:</p>
    <address>
